msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes.rst:221
msgid "Can a single executable contain more than one node?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes.rst:222
msgid ""
"Yes. In ROS, a single executable, such as a C++ or Python program, can "
"contain one or more nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes.rst:225
msgid "Why does another Turtlesim window open when I remap the node name?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes.rst:226
msgid ""
"Each call to ``ros2 run turtlesim turtlesim_node`` starts a new node, and "
"Turtlesim opens a window for it. Remapping ``__node`` sets the name of that "
"new node. It does not rename or replace the ``/turtlesim`` node that is "
"already running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes.rst:230
msgid ""
"What is the difference between ``ros2 node list`` and ``ros2 node info``?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes.rst:231
msgid ""
"``ros2 node list`` shows the names of all running nodes. ``ros2 node info`` "
"shows the connections of a single node, including its publishers, "
"subscribers, services, and actions."
msgstr ""
